# Per-model environment for glm-5.3 (Zhipu / Z.ai) via Z.ai's
# Anthropic-compatible endpoint. Copy to env/glm-5.3.env and fill in the key.
# The real .env file is gitignored; never commit keys.
#
# Docs: https://docs.z.ai/scenario-example/develop-tools/claude
# Note (verified 2026-08-15): that setup guide is two generations stale — it
# names GLM-4.7 and GLM-4.5-Air as the Claude Code defaults, and says nothing
# about the thinking requirement below. The GLM Coding Plan is documented as
# using this same base URL and the same ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN variable as
# pay-as-you-go; there is no separate coding-plan endpoint.
ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://api.z.ai/api/anthropic
ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=REPLACE_ME
# Pin every internal model slot to glm-5.3 so no side-channel calls
# (subagents, background summarization) leak to a different vendor/model.
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=glm-5.3
ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL=glm-5.3
ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_SONNET_MODEL=glm-5.3
ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL=glm-5.3
CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL=glm-5.3

# --- RETRACTED: "glm-5.3 requires a thinking block" ---
#
# On 2026-08-15 ~04:39Z, with NO active plan on the key, glm-5.3 returned HTTP
# 400 code 1210 ("This model always engages in thinking and cannot be disabled;
# please use low, high, or max") for every request shape EXCEPT those carrying
# an explicit `thinking` block. That looked like a hard model constraint.
#
# It is not. At ~05:00Z, with a GLM Coding Plan attached to the same key, every
# shape succeeds -- including no `thinking` field at all and
# `thinking: {"type":"disabled"}`. The 1210 appears to be an account-state
# artifact, not a request-shape rule.
#
# Do not rely on either reading for pay-as-you-go accounts: that path could not
# be retested, because the pay-go balance was exhausted throughout. The only
# safe statement is that with an active coding plan, request shape is
# unconstrained.
#
# Lesson recorded because it nearly shipped: a 400 observed under a broken
# credential is a fact about the credential until it reproduces under a working
# one.
#
# --- ROUTING: version pins are NOT honoured (verified, 5/5 stable) ---
#
# On the coding plan this endpoint silently resolves a requested model to a
# newer one. See analysis/2026-08-15-glm53-routing/routing.txt.
#     glm-5.2, glm-5.1, glm-5  -> served glm-5.3
#     glm-4.5-air              -> served glm-4.7
#     claude-opus-4-8/sonnet   -> served glm-4.7   (documented shim behaviour)
#     unknown model id         -> 400 code 1214, so IDs *are* validated
# Nothing errors and nothing warns. The only signal is the `model` field on the
# response. Any version-pinned comparison run through this endpoint is invalid
# unless every run's served model string is recorded and checked.
